    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide\">Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide</a></i> </p><p><i>See also:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Force_Secrets\" title=\"Force Secrets\">Force Secrets</a></i> </p><p>When you use a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Force_Power\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Force Power\">Force Power</a> that affects targets within an area (such as a radius or a cone), you can spend a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Force_Point\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Force Point\">Force Point</a> to double the distance that the effect extends from your square (for example, a 6-square cone can be made into a 12-square cone). Alternatively, you can spend a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Destiny_Point\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Destiny Point\">Destiny Point</a> to multiply the distance the effect extends by 5 (making a 6-square cone into a 30-square cone). </p>",
